Subject: [PATCH v9 10/10] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec the Next, Later, and
 quarantine folders
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: xlunvnzsqsvlpvpmzoomywrowwpymvzx
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:05:07 +0000

Pat triages the list in three steps, not two: a message is either
done, needs work soon, or can wait. INBOX and Archive alone cannot hold
that middle state anywhere every client and agent sees it, and a
notmuch tag cannot either, since it is not in the list data and a
rebuilt index loses it. Mail from a sender the agent must not act on
needs a place of its own for the same reason.

Next, Later, and quarantine are folders like Archive, so the state
travels with the message through lab-mail and Fastmail. lab-mail
carries every folder already, so only the clients name them. The spec
makes the folder the only state: clients derive their tags from it,
and a move is the one way to change it, from Emacs or Fastmail's web
interface alike.

The spec also turns flag sync on for Pat's notmuch, so read, flagged,
and answered match Fastmail and notmuch serves as a full client of the
account. It stays off for the agent, whose login cannot set flags.
